{"id": "clm:2251c263a3f8aec1d0f9777efda99d7b4ecc42e0ae992f9e035df0f54feb0eca", "type": "statement", "text": "Inspect pg_index.indisvalid for query eligibility and indisready for INSERT/UPDATE maintenance; indisready=false means writes ignore the index, so invalid does not imply one universal maintenance state. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/catalog-pg-index.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PostgreSQL invalid indexes from failed CONCURRENTLY builds"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d81d60b66bb35c875a8ac479f1085d6acf03e018b118707aafcbed4bde769655", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bb9a21a06d250a2c60cd6d0c7920acf6557479f6b7cdf8e70b37e8c3e2509566"]}
{"id": "clm:90df273bab49a11e2c06fae5a5f9f9b14afb63f425a26e858c376d820e0dce2b", "type": "statement", "text": "Deadlocks or uniqueness errors during concurrent scanning can leave invalid indexes that queries cannot use; pganalyze independently documents failed or aborted concurrent builds as a typical cause. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-createindex.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PostgreSQL invalid indexes from failed CONCURRENTLY builds"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.dbi-services.com/blog/create-index-concurrently-in-postgresql/", "https://pganalyze.com/docs/checks/schema/index_invalid"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d81d60b66bb35c875a8ac479f1085d6acf03e018b118707aafcbed4bde769655", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:a001d3487b1425b7c8b1eea516eba1218351641b561923d2404a0d574104f9bd", "type": "statement", "text": "A unique concurrent build starts enforcing uniqueness during its second scan; failure there can leave uniqueness enforcement active even though queries cannot use the index. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-createindex.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PostgreSQL invalid indexes from failed CONCURRENTLY builds"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/catalog-pg-index.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d81d60b66bb35c875a8ac479f1085d6acf03e018b118707aafcbed4bde769655", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:2bad76d575e9f947aab3e268c116f76cd45957fff945ac4da4c4de831482a419", "type": "statement", "text": "Blind retries can fail with relation already exists; IF NOT EXISTS only checks name existence and cannot establish that the existing index is usable or matches the intended definition. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-createindex.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PostgreSQL invalid indexes from failed CONCURRENTLY builds"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.dbi-services.com/blog/create-index-concurrently-in-postgresql/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d81d60b66bb35c875a8ac479f1085d6acf03e018b118707aafcbed4bde769655", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:1885cca27ba49c10f387d54954a9b670e5705e2299c46378a64b0d19baabc27e", "type": "statement", "text": "A running concurrent build is initially invalid too; indisvalid=false alone cannot establish that creation has failed. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-createindex.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PostgreSQL invalid indexes from failed CONCURRENTLY builds"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github-wiki-see.page/m/FullmetalBober/Indexterity/wiki/Architecture"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d81d60b66bb35c875a8ac479f1085d6acf03e018b118707aafcbed4bde769655", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:c1a7b31393e517542bd9441290e0784c31277d7de75f544852b1af0bd381e5a1"]}
{"id": "clm:d83f4cbeccf3c0be7729bb6187c2458cc8d338a8651be52026920bcf810b2e27", "type": "statement", "text": "Concurrent creation uses multiple transactions; cancellation after catalog creation can leave an INVALID index, unlike an aborted ordinary build. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-createindex.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PostgreSQL invalid indexes from failed CONCURRENTLY builds"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.dbi-services.com/blog/create-index-concurrently-in-postgresql/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d81d60b66bb35c875a8ac479f1085d6acf03e018b118707aafcbed4bde769655", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:c1a7b31393e517542bd9441290e0784c31277d7de75f544852b1af0bd381e5a1", "ev:d1b351b66088e3d939bd8e14c35433633f98738a8f12e4c931c98991a5aa396c"]}
{"id": "clm:a4940b32a70b577b09b0c583c029a5d3a858f763952b5cbf8141a3ae259416b4", "type": "statement", "text": "Invalid artifacts can occupy disk and incur write maintenance despite providing no query acceleration; dbi demonstrates a sequential scan and subsequent index growth. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-createindex.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PostgreSQL invalid indexes from failed CONCURRENTLY builds"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.dbi-services.com/blog/create-index-concurrently-in-postgresql/", "https://pganalyze.com/docs/checks/schema/index_invalid"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d81d60b66bb35c875a8ac479f1085d6acf03e018b118707aafcbed4bde769655", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6fdb1032d0a74c8dcf28c11bec24d7bc8155df860569305372b507e07f8d0494"]}
{"id": "clm:9cac9a7eb51814149e4ce0f13f704729f34ce9ad91651da7a831bf2637d00334", "type": "statement", "text": "Drop and recreate a failed index, or use REINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY; the latter is the REINDEX form that can concurrently rebuild an invalid index. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-createindex.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PostgreSQL invalid indexes from failed CONCURRENTLY builds"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-reindex.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d81d60b66bb35c875a8ac479f1085d6acf03e018b118707aafcbed4bde769655", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:7401998c0f75815409147c926907321c50f54e4411870484d631849196e324cb", "type": "statement", "text": "After failed concurrent reindexing, an INVALID _ccnew artifact represents the unfinished replacement; drop it and retry. An INVALID _ccold artifact is the old index left after successful rebuilding; drop it. Numeric suffixes may follow these names. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-reindex.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["PostgreSQL invalid indexes from failed CONCURRENTLY builds"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:d81d60b66bb35c875a8ac479f1085d6acf03e018b118707aafcbed4bde769655", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
